Vendored packages under this directory
=======================================

github.com/danos/godbus/dbus (from golang-github-godbus-dbus, formerly
golang-dbus) and github.com/danos/objtree (from
golang-github-jsouthworth-objtree) are vendored here, under a private
import path, instead of being separate Build-Depends.

Why: dbus_transport.go uses this project's fork of godbus/dbus 4.0.0
(github.com/godbus/dbus, unversioned import path), which adds a
server-side Handler/SignalHandler extension API. Debian trixie's own
golang-dbus-dev (5.1.0, github.com/godbus/dbus/v5) is needed
transitively by golang-go-systemd-dev, which services.go imports
directly. Both packages install their Go sources to the same physical
path under /usr/share/gocode/src/github.com/godbus/dbus/ (Debian's own
packaging quirk, not a versioned subdirectory), so they cannot be
installed in the same build root at the same time: "dpkg: trying to
overwrite '.../godbus/dbus/auth.go', which is also in package
golang-dbus-dev (5.1.0-1)".

Vendoring the v4 fork under a path Debian's packaging never touches
(github.com/danos/godbus/dbus, not github.com/godbus/dbus) avoids the
collision without touching the Handler/SignalHandler API (confirmed
present with identical signatures in real upstream v5 by comparing
against github.com/godbus/dbus v5.1.0 directly) or vci's own dbus
semantics.

github.com/danos/objtree is vendored alongside it, pointed at the same
private dbus path, because objtree.NewAnonymousBusManager's own
function signature (func(dbus.Handler, dbus.SignalHandler) (*dbus.Conn,
error)) requires exact Go type identity with whichever dbus package the
caller uses -- vci could not pass its own connectFn to the real,
separately-packaged objtree without both agreeing on the same dbus
import path.

Both copies carry this project's own patches
(golang-github-godbus-dbus's synchronous-send.patch and
parse-dbus-address-correctly.patch) applied directly, since there is no
quilt series for a vendor/ tree.

If either upstream (or this project's own fork) changes, refresh both
copies from their source packages and reapply the note above; they are
not expected to drift from golang-github-godbus-dbus and
golang-github-jsouthworth-objtree's own git history otherwise.
